{"deviations":[{"source":"docs/verification/vv-plan.md","text":"**F02 reference (after the first registered run, on independent review).** The independent volume calculation originally obtained the line-of-sight distance per direction from `Scene3D.intersect`, the same routine the field-of-view code uses, so a geometry error common to both could not have been detected. The reference now enumerates box-face planes and the ground plane directly. The registered criterion (`effective_volume_matches_independent_3pct`) and its 3 % threshold are unchanged; the result with the original reference is kept in `metrics.json` (`rel_diff_scene_reference`) next to the new one, and convergence diagnostics (half-sample Monte Carlo, quadrature refinement) are reported for every case."},{"source":"docs/verification/vv-plan.md","text":"**M01 gate (on the same review).** The registry criterion checked only that the media files exist, while this plan also promised that the error drawn equals the record. The criterion `drawn_error_matches_record` was added to the registry and the experiment (the drawn curve is the recorded error floored at 1 mm for the logarithmic axis); the PDF is now checked like the videos. The media content is the top-view version described above (the earlier draft of this plan mentioned an entropy panel and a 3D keyframe figure, which were not built)."},{"source":"docs/verification/vv-plan.md","text":"**F01 (on the same review).** The waveform simulator and the analytic model are compared on the same traced record, so F01 tests the model given the radiometry, not the radiometry itself. A hand-written E7–E8 power for each cell is now reported next to the traced power (`power_rel_error_vs_hand`); no gate was added."},{"source":"docs/verification/vv-plan.md","text":"**Provenance.** `run.json` records the revision, modified tracked files and a hash of all sources before the experiment code is loaded and again afterwards; trial caches carry a fingerprint of the job that produced them. The first runs of F01, F02 and M01 predate this and were repeated from the final revision (same seeds, identical numerical results where the experiment code did not change)."}],"experiments":[{"criteria":[{"key":"crossing_rate_in_simultaneous_wilson","supported":true,"text":"predicted P_D inside the Bonferroni (familywise 99 %) Wilson interval of the simulated crossing rate in every cell"},{"key":"high_snr_std_ratio_within_5pct","supported":true,"text":"for cells with P_D > 0.999999 and wrap probability < 1e-6, unwrap-free range std / sigma_R within 1 +/- 0.05"},{"key":"false_report_rate_in_wilson99","supported":true,"text":"predicted P_FA |W| / L_c inside the 99 % Wilson interval of the no-return report rate (clear air and sunlight)"}],"exploratory":false,"id":"F01","observations":[{"label":"Cells","source":"OUT/F01/metrics.json","unit":"","value":60},{"label":"High-SNR cells","source":"OUT/F01/metrics.json","unit":"","value":26},{"label":"Largest crossing-rate gap","source":"OUT/F01/metrics.json","unit":"","value":0.015039495433572914}],"provenance":{"seed":5111,"sourceSha256":"d9c94c172a4db7ecbb2aa10e6a8339b6d6a645cdab8fd6020db0ea2a310341ff","timestamp":"2026-11-18T03:39:44.050545+00:00"},"source":"OUT/F01/metrics.json","title":"3D measurement model against the waveform truth"},{"criteria":[{"key":"nested_geometric_los_effective","supported":true,"text":"effective subset of line-of-sight subset of geometric for every sampled point, pose, probe and condition"},{"key":"black_volume_clear_gt_fog_gt_sun","supported":true,"text":"black-probe effective volume ordered clear > fog > sunlight at every pose"},{"key":"effective_volume_matches_independent_3pct","supported":true,"text":"Monte Carlo effective volume within 3 % of the independent direction quadrature with r_50 from the midterm calibration formulas"},{"key":"moving_origin_range_error_below_1e-9","supported":true,"text":"traced ranges equal the analytic moving-origin ranges within 1e-9 m at every sp